{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>On the first day of the first month, on the first of the month, you shall set up the Tabernacle of the Tent of Meeting.</b> According to the view of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, Moses would set it up and take it apart three times each day, as it says הוקם, תקים, ויקם — one for the morning daily offering, one for the inauguration offerings, and one for the afternoon daily offering. And in this parashah you will find these three erections: ״תקים את משכן אהל מועד״, and it is written ״הוקם המשכן״, and after it is written ״ויקם משה את המשכן״." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> Bezalel and Oholiab and every wise-hearted man were toiling to set it up and it would not stand, and this is what the verse says: ״ויביאו את המשכן אל משה״ — and this was distressing to him because he had no portion in the Tabernacle. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: It is impossible for its erection to be by the hand of flesh and blood; rather, you engage with it and it will stand up on its own, so that all Israel may know that if it does not stand up through you, it will never stand up for all eternity. And I am writing its erection under your name, as it says: ״ביום החדש הראשון באחד לחדש תקים את משכן״. Moses said: Master of the Universe, I do not know how to set it up! He said to him: Engage with your hand, and you are fitting to set it up, and it will stand on its own, as it says: ״הוקם המשכן״. And I inscribe its erection under your name, as it says: ״ויקם משה את המשכן״. This is what the verse says (Psalms 45:15): ״לרקמות תובל למלך״ — 'with embroideries the king's consort is brought in.' This is the Tabernacle, which was depicted in embroidery, as it says (Exodus 35:35): ״ורוקם בתכלת ובארגמן״. ״תובל למלך״ — 'is brought to the king' — this is Moses, as it says (Deuteronomy 33:5): ״ויהי בישורון מלך״. ״בתולות אחריה״ — 'the maidens behind her' — these are Israel, who are called maidens, as it says (Song of Songs 4:12): ״גן נעול אחותי כלה״. ״רעותיה״ — 'her companions' — who are friends to the Holy One, blessed be He, as it says (Psalms 122:8): ״למען אחי וריעי״. ״מובאות לך״ — 'are brought to you' — that they brought the Tabernacle to Moses."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:08:07.289664170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}